  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Uganda SRL and other Countries to Improve TB diagnosis in the ECSA Region - Africa - Multicountry Africa ECSA-HC (01-Nov-2015-30-Jun-2019)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multicountry Africa ECSA-HC, Tuberculosis, East, Central and Southern Africa Health Community (ECSA-HC)This program has the following goals: Build a regional network of National TB reference Laboratories (NRLs) for inter-state laboratory quality assurance and management in the ECSA countries.  Enhanced impact of rapid molecular TB diagnostic testings in the region and building capacity of NRLs to undertake epidemiological/national level- disease monitoring surveys such as DRS and TB disease prevalence.  Improved Laboratory service provision for quality assured 1st and 2nd line Drug susceptibility testing accessible to needed people of the ECSA region. The objectives of this program are: Objective 1: To Establish a regional network of 18 National TB Reference Laboratires in sub-saharan Africa (among ECSA states).  Objective 2: To provide quality trainings to NRL lab staff of 18 countries and to provide Supranational TB Reference laboratory (SNRL) services to the region- prioritized by country needs.  Objective 3: To provide technical support for conducting anti-TB Drug resistance surveillance, TB prevalence surveys, and Expansion of rapid TB diagnostic testing</narrative>
  </description>
